WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.788
Over five hundred billion dollars in federal COVID-19 spending between 2020 and 2023.

00:00:06.738 --> 00:00:14.068
Two hundred and thirty-four point five billion in emergency measures — the Canada Emergency Response Benefit as the primary component.

00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:17.886
Six point nine billion in confirmed CERB fraud.

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:21.124
Four point three million dollars paid to inmates.

00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:24.920
One point four billion dollars sent to people outside Canada.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.545
Less than one percent of fraudulent claims have been recovered.

00:00:28.545 --> 00:00:34.522
The government created the largest emergency spending program in Canadian history — then failed to audit it.

00:00:34.522 --> 00:00:38.363
Contracts awarded without competitive bidding during the emergency.

00:00:38.363 --> 00:00:42.397
Department-to-department coordination failures throughout the response.

00:00:42.397 --> 00:00:45.556
Zero accountability for fraud perpetrators.

00:00:45.556 --> 00:00:47.886
Five hundred billion spent.

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:49.704
The money is gone.

00:00:49.704 --> 00:00:52.045
The accounting is incomplete.

00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:54.670
And no one is asking where it went.
